   "fen": "r3kb1r/1b1n1ppp/4p3/1pp1P3/3p1B2/3P1N2/PP3PPP/RN3RK1 b kq - 1 16",
   "line": [
    "d4",
    "Bf4"
   ],
   "spoken": "The key decision: capture the knight or not. Taking it is committal — you surrender a monster bishop — but it permanently cripples the opponent's pawns. In a slow game you might keep the bishop, but the capture is probably objectively best, and it teaches a lovely follow-up.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 32,
   "t": 1844,
