   "line": [
    "g5"
   ],
   "spoken": "The opponent wants to retreat the bishop and prop the weakness with a pawn to f4. There are two answers: the textbook route reroutes the knight to the fine central square, or the spicier pawn thrust to g5 — untouchable because a rook capture would recapture — which draws the sting from f4 and makes the central weakness permanent.",
   "kind": "plan"
